course: dictionary
lesson: 8948
title: Silliness and context
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Silliness is a noun. It names a way of behaving that is foolish, funny or not serious. Teachers sometimes say, «That's enough silliness», when a class is being too playful to get on with its work.
explain: Silliness can also mean a silly act or silly talk. Context tells you which meaning fits. Read the words around it and ask: is this behaviour playful, or is it causing a problem?
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mad Hatter's tea party is full of silliness, but it is also clever nonsense. So here the silliness is playful fun. Silliness can be happy like that, but it can also be annoying or unsafe, so the clues in the sentence matter.
fact: Silliness is a noun: it names a way of behaving.
fact: «Silliness» means behaving in a foolish, funny or not serious way.
fact: «Folly» is an old word that means silliness.
fact: Silliness can be playful and happy, or annoying and unsafe.
fact: In Alice in Wonderland, the Mad Hatter's tea party is full of silliness that is also clever nonsense.
exercise: «That's enough silliness, class.» What does silliness mean here? | Quiet reading time | *Silly behaviour that is stopping the work | A kind of weather | Clever ideas that help us learn
exercise: Which word is an old word for silliness? | Pettishly | Penitence | Appreciated | *Folly
exercise: In Alice in Wonderland, the tea party is full of silliness that is also clever nonsense. What does this tell you? | Nobody talks at all | The party is very sad | *The silliness is playful fun | The guests are all asleep
test: Silliness can be harmful. Which example is unsafe silliness? | Laughing at a joke | Drawing a picture | *Messing about on a busy road | Singing a song
test: What does «folly» mean? | Being sorry | *Silliness | Household rubbish | Valued
exam: Ella says silliness is always bad. What is the best answer? | Silliness is a kind of weather | *Not always: silliness can be playful and happy, or unsafe | Silliness means being very quiet | Yes, silliness is always bad and must be stopped
